-- The last file of a chain of three: it imports
-- ok/section-given-import-contract-mid.l4, which imports
-- ok/section-given-import-contract-def.l4, and names a contract that is itself
-- built from an imported one as an operand of RAND (smucclaw/l4-ide#1118).
-- `both sides` reads a section GIVEN of its own and, through `pay leg`, one of
-- the file two steps away. It is used here as an operand, on its own, and
-- beside `bob first`, which has the imported contract as its HENCE. The last
-- trace is of `plain mid`, a rule of the middle file that has the imported
-- contract as an operand of RAND and is traced only from here.

IMPORT `section-given-import-contract-mid`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`and a third` MEANS
    `both sides`
    RAND
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 12)

#TRACE `and a third` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`just both sides` MEANS `both sides`

#TRACE `just both sides` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`first, as an operand` MEANS
    `bob first`
    RAND
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 12)

#TRACE `first, as an operand` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 3
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 9
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `plain mid` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30
